From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haseenesss <Haseenesss@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:47:11 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Mac app: an update without control data gets no base game
 version

A dump, or a NUP update without a NACP, carries no control data, so the
app version fell back to the base game's control data, or to 1.0 for a
dump. The Mac app then named a version that does not run: Donkey Kong
Bananza packed with update v458752 said 1.0.

The app version is now the packed version's own display version, else
the version number the profile registers for its main build, and the
base game's only when the base game is packed. pack_app.py writes it
as DMDisplayVersion, and the packed version as DMPackageVersion
(v458752), which is all an update without control data has.

Front-ends: show DMDisplayVersion, else DMPackageVersion, before
CFBundleShortVersionString, which is 1.0 for an update without control
data (docs/frontends.md).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#1784
Reason: An update packed from a dump or a NUP named the base game's version, or 1.0, in the Mac app; the launcher shows the version that runs
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#953

