 ## Starting a game
 
-**A Mac app** is started like any app, or by running its `Contents/MacOS/nxnative` with the chosen settings in its environment (`DM_FPS_TARGET=30`, …). The launcher there runs the host as a child, forwards SIGTERM, SIGINT and SIGHUP to it and exits with its exit code: 0 for a quit (⌘Q, the Home prompt, closing the window), 70 after the alert that macOS stopped running the game's GPU work ([A GPU whose access macOS revoked stops the game](reference/rendering.md#a-gpu-whose-access-macos-revoked-stops-the-game)), 134 for an abort. A variable already in the environment wins; then come `~/Library/Application Support/nxnative/<title ID>/env.txt` and the bundle's `dm/env.txt`, one `KEY=VALUE` per line ([A Mac app](development.md#a-mac-app)). The save is in `save/` in that Application Support folder; the log is `~/Library/Logs/nxnative/<title ID>.log`, the previous run's `<title ID>.prev.log`. The title ID is `DMTitleID` in the app's `Info.plist`.
+**A Mac app** is started like any app, or by running its `Contents/MacOS/nxnative` with the chosen settings in its environment (`DM_FPS_TARGET=30`, …). The launcher there runs the host as a child, forwards SIGTERM, SIGINT and SIGHUP to it and exits with its exit code: 0 for a quit (⌘Q, the Home prompt, closing the window), 70 after the alert that macOS stopped running the game's GPU work ([A GPU whose access macOS revoked stops the game](reference/rendering.md#a-gpu-whose-access-macos-revoked-stops-the-game)), 134 for an abort. A variable already in the environment wins; then come `~/Library/Application Support/nxnative/<title ID>/env.txt` and the bundle's `dm/env.txt`, one `KEY=VALUE` per line ([A Mac app](development.md#a-mac-app)). The save is in `save/` in that Application Support folder; the log is `~/Library/Logs/nxnative/<title ID>.log`, the previous run's `<title ID>.prev.log`. The title ID is `DMTitleID` in the app's `Info.plist`. Its game version is `DMDisplayVersion` (the packed version's display version, 1.2.1), else `DMPackageVersion` (the packed version, v458752): an update packed without control data, from a dump or a NUP, has no display version, and `CFBundleShortVersionString` is then 1.0, not the version that runs. An app packed before these keys has `CFBundleShortVersionString` alone.
 
 A Mac app shows its own settings window before the game, drawn from its `launcher.json` and keeping its choices in the same store ([Saved choices](#saved-choices), [The Mac settings window](settings.md#the-mac-settings-window)). It shows a variable the launch environment or an `env.txt` sets as fixed. A front end that draws the settings itself starts the app with `DM_LAUNCHER=0` in its environment (or `--no-launcher` on its command line) to skip the window. The saved choices still apply, so a front end that writes them gets the same game as the window would. With `DM_PREFLIGHT` set in its environment the app exits at once, before it reads anything, rolls its log or touches the saves: a front end opens a new build that way (through LaunchServices, `NSWorkspace.openApplication`), so macOS runs its first-start check of the bundle then, not when the player starts the game. The check scans every file of an ad hoc signed app and takes minutes with a RomFS of several GB, and macOS remembers it until the app changes.
 
